    affiliation: "Duke University School of Medicine, Department of Surgery"

version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-07"

repository-code: "https://github.com/Duke-Vascular-Informatics/pad-amp-nhd-val"
url: "https://github.com/Duke-Vascular-Informatics/pad-amp-nhd-val"

license: GPL-3.0

abstract: >
  A Strategus-based OMOP CDM v5.4 observational study externally validating
  three published integer risk scores — Iannuzzi 2020, Subramaniam 2018 mFI-5,
  and Kraiss 2022 sVQI-FS — against non-home discharge after major lower
  extremity amputation. Each score is evaluated for discrimination (AUROC,
  AUPRC) and calibration (Brier score, expected calibration error, calibration
  intercept/slope), including a subgroup differential-performance (bias)
  assessment across demographic and clinical strata. This repository is a
  frozen, validation-only fork of pad-amp-nhd-prog, made to keep the analysis
  underlying a publication stable while pad-amp-nhd-prog continues toward a
  de-novo risk score.
  Funding: Research reported in this publication was supported by the National
  Center For Advancing Translational Sciences of the National Institutes of
  Health under Award Number K12TR005435. The content is solely the
  responsibility of the authors and does not necessarily represent the
  official views of the National Institutes of Health.

keywords:
  - OMOP CDM
  - OHDSI
  - Strategus
  - external validation
  - risk score
  - non-home discharge
  - amputation
  - clinical informatics
  - FeatureExtraction
  - R

